-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/789fe39a-953f-5652-b18c-abd5f164035e
-- title:
--   Function field embeds into Γ'-invariants via chartwise meromorphic pull-backs
-- statement:
--   **Base data.** Let $r$ be a prime; let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain, assumed to be a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), let $\pi\in\mathcal O$ be irreducible (`hπ`), let $\mathcal O$ be complete for the $\pi$-adic filtration (`hcomplete`), let $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ have exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and let $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficients.** Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra, and $\mathrm{Fr}$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of it, subject to: $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo that ideal (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo that ideal for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** Let $v\!\det\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) be a group homomorphism such that $v\!\det(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma\colon G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism and $\Gamma\le G$ a subgroup such that some $z\in\Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix with $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$ (`hcent`) and some $w\in\Gamma$ has $v\!\det(\sigma w)=1$ (`hodd`); let $\Gamma'\le G$ be the subgroup characterised by: $x\in\Gamma'$ iff $x\in\Gamma$ and $v\!\det(\sigma x)$ is even (`hΓ'`). Let $\rho\colon G\to \mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ be the homomorphism sending $g$ to the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`), and assume that on the vertex set $\mathrm{Vertex}\,\mathcal O\,K_0$ (homothety classes of full $\mathcal O$-lattices in $K_0^2$) each vertex has finite stabiliser in the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hdisc`) and that some finite set of vertices meets every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The quotient datum.** Let $\mathcal X$ be a scheme and $f\colon\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ proper and flat. Write $\Omega=\,$`Omega K₀ π` for the functor sending an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ to the Deligne data over $B$, i.e. families of $B$-submodules $\mathrm{line}(M)\subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}M$ indexed by the full lattices $M\subset K_0^2$ with invertible quotient, monotone under inclusion of lattices, equivariant for homothety matrices, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$ (five clauses, summarised here); write $\mathrm{corep}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ for $B\mapsto \operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O\text{-alg}}(O^{\mathrm{nr}},B)$ and $\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,f$ for $B\mapsto\{\varphi\colon \operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal X \mid \varphi\ \text{followed by}\ f=\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O\to B)\}$. Let $\Theta$ assign, to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map from pairs $(\psi,P)$ with $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ to such $B$-points of $\mathcal X$, subject to four hypotheses: $\Theta$ commutes with the functorial maps along $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms (`hΘnat`); $\Theta$ is invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action, i.e. $\Theta(x')=\Theta(x)$ whenever `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` holds for $\sigma\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma$, which says $x'_1=x_1\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ is the $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$-pull-back of $x_2$ lattice by lattice (`hΘinv`); for every algebraically closed field $k$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$, the map $P\mapsto\Theta(\psi,P)$ is onto the $k$-points of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and two data have the same image precisely when they are related by the twisted action of some $\gamma\in\Gamma$ (`hΘfib`); and $\Theta$ is initial among such families: for every $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every natural $\Gamma$-invariant family $\rho'$ of $T$-valued points there is a natural transformation $u$ of $\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,f$ into $\mathrm{nilpPoints}\,t$ with $u\circ\Theta=\rho'$, unique among natural transformations with that property (`hΘuniv`).
--
--   **Analytic frame.** Let $C$ be a field and $K_0$-algebra, carrying a valuation with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, complete and algebraically closed. Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a subalgebra-of-scalars for $C$ (scalar towers $\mathcal O\to R\to C$ and $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$). Let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformizer of $C$ over $K_0$, that is, an element $\varpi.\varpi\in K_0$ whose valuation in $C$ lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and such that every nonzero element of $K_0$ is squeezed between two powers of it. Let `hF : IsAdicFrame π ϖ R` hold: $\pi$ is irreducible, $R\to C$ is injective, its image is exactly $\{c\in C: v(c)\le 1\}$, $R$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, an element of $K_0$ has valuation $\le 1$ in $C$ iff it lies in the image of $\mathcal O$, the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and the images of $\pi$ and of $\varpi.\varpi$ in $C$ agree. Let $\psi_0\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism. Assume the valuation has rank one in the form: for $x,y\in C$ with $v(x)<1$ and $y\neq 0$ there is $n$ with $v(x)^n\le v(y)$ (`hrk`); that every nonzero $\varepsilon\in\Gamma_0$ dominates $v(y)$ for some $y\neq0$ (`hval`); that the affinoids exhaust the Drinfeld upper half plane $\Omega=\{z\in C: z\notin\mathrm{im}(K_0)\}$, each $z\in\Omega$ lying in some $\mathrm{affinoid}\,\varpi\,n=\{z: v(z)\le v(\varpi)^{-n}$ and $v(z-a)\ge v(\varpi)^{n}$ for all $a\in K_0$ with $v(a)\le v(\varpi)^{-n}\}$ (`hex`); and that the ring $\mathrm{HolRingOf}\,\varpi\,\rho$ is a domain, this ring being the subring `holRing ϖ` of functions $\Omega\to C$ whose restriction to each affinoid is a uniformly bounded uniform limit of values of rational functions with no poles there.
--
--   **Uniformisation of adic points.** Let $\Phi$ send each adic point $x$ (a compatible system of Deligne data $x.\mathrm{pt}\,n$ over $R/(\pi^{n+1})$) to an $R$-point $p$ of $\mathcal X$ with $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O\to R)$, and let `hΦ` hold, a conjunction of four clauses: for every $x$ and $n$, the reduction of $\Phi(x)$ along $R\to R/(\pi^{n+1})$ is the point $\Theta(\psi_0 \bmod \pi^{n+1},\,x.\mathrm{pt}\,n)$; $\Phi$ is surjective; $\Phi(x)=\Phi(x')$ if and only if $x'=x.\mathrm{act}(\sigma\gamma)$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma'$; and base change along $R\to C$ is injective on such $R$-points and hits every $C$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Base change to $C$.** Let $s_C\colon\operatorname{Spec}C\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be the morphism induced by $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$ (`hsC`), and assume the fibre product $\mathcal X_C=\mathcal X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}C$ is integral. For a morphism $q\colon\operatorname{Spec}C\to\mathcal X_C$ and an open $U$ of $\mathcal X_C$ with $\top\le q^{-1}U$, write $s(q)\in C$ for the value of a section $s$ over $U$, obtained by pulling $s$ back along $q$, restricting to $\top$ and using the global-sections identification for $\operatorname{Spec}C$.
--
--   **Chartwise meromorphy.** Assume `hmero`: for every open $U\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ containing the generic point and every $s\in\mathcal O_{\mathcal X_C}(U)$ there is a function $F\colon\Omega\to C$ with four properties. (a) For every adic point $x$, every $z\in\Omega$ with $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ and every $q\colon\operatorname{Spec}C\to\mathcal X_C$ whose composite with the first projection is the base change of $\Phi(x)$ along $R\to C$ and whose composite with the second projection is the identity, and with $\top\le q^{-1}U$, one has $F(z)=s(q)$. (b) $F(w)=F(z)$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ and $w=\mathrm{pmoebius}(\rho\gamma)(z)$ for $z,w\in\Omega$. (c) For each $n$ there are $a,b$ holomorphic on $\mathrm{affinoid}\,\varpi\,n$ with $b$ not identically zero there and $b(z)F(z)=a(z)$ at every point of the affinoid where $b(z)\neq0$. (d) For every $x$, $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ and $q$ as in (a) with $\top\le q^{-1}U$, there are $N$, a disc $D=\{w: v(w-z)\le v(\varpi)^{N}\}$ contained in $\Omega$, and functions $a,b$ holomorphic on $D$ with $b$ nonzero at $z$ and $b(w)F(w)=a(w)$ for all $w\in D$.
--
--   **Finiteness of bad points.** Assume `hfin`: for every open $U$ containing the generic point and every $n$, the set of $z$ in $\mathrm{affinoid}\,\varpi\,n$ of the form $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ for some adic point $x$ admitting a $q$ as in (a) for which $\top\le q^{-1}U$ fails, is finite.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a ring homomorphism $e$ from the function field of $\mathcal X_C$ (the stalk at its generic point) to the subfield $\mathrm{invariantFieldOf}\,C\,G\,(\mathrm{HolRingOf}\,\varpi\,\rho)\,\Gamma'$ of the fraction field of $\mathrm{HolRingOf}\,\varpi\,\rho$, consisting of those elements fixed by every $\gamma\in\Gamma'$, such that:
--
--   (i) $e$ is the identity on constants: for every $c\in C$, $e$ applied to the image of $c$ under $\mathrm{baseToFunctionField}$ of the second projection $\mathcal X_C\to\operatorname{Spec}C$ equals the image of $c$ under the structure map of $C$ into that invariant subfield;
--
--   (ii) for every open $U\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ containing the generic point and every section $s$ over $U$ there are $a,b\in \mathrm{HolRingOf}\,\varpi\,\rho$ with $b$ a non-zero-divisor such that, first, the image of $e$ applied to the germ of $s$ at the generic point, viewed in the fraction field, is the fraction $a/b$, and second, for every adic point $x$, every $z\in\Omega$ with $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ and every $q\colon\operatorname{Spec}C\to\mathcal X_C$ whose composite with the first projection is the base change of $\Phi(x)$ along $R\to C$ and whose composite with the second projection is the identity, with $\top\le q^{-1}U$, the functions $a,b$ on $\Omega$ satisfy $b(z)\cdot s(q)=a(z)$.
--
--   This is the analytic half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: it manufactures the evaluation homomorphism from the function field of the base-changed curve $\mathcal X_C$ into the $\Gamma'$-invariant subfield of the fraction field of the ring of rigid holomorphic functions on Drinfeld's upper half plane, given that each germ pulls back along the uniformisation $\Phi$ to a $\Gamma'$-invariant function that is meromorphic on every affinoid chart and near every uniformised point. It feeds the step [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_invariantFieldOf_eval_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient_of_smooth`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_invariantFieldOf_eval_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient_of_smooth), where the chartwise meromorphy hypotheses are supplied from smoothness of the quotient datum.
